@startuml comunicacao-comprar-ingresso
!include _estilo-comum.puml

title Diagrama de Comunicação\nUC13 - Comprar Ingresso

skinparam actorStyle awesome

actor "Comprador" as BUY
boundary "Checkout (UI)"  as UI
control  "Elo API"        as API
control  "OrderService"   as ORD
control  "PaymentService" as PAY
control  "TicketService"  as TCK
queue    "Cloud Tasks"    as Q
control  "Worker"         as WRK
boundary "Gateway Pag."   as GW
boundary "Resend"         as MAIL
database "PostgreSQL"     as DB

BUY  --> UI  : 1: iniciarPedido(eventId, itens)
UI   --> API : 2: POST /orders
API  --> ORD : 3: criarPedido()
ORD  --> DB  : 4: salvarPedido(PENDENTE)
BUY  --> UI  : 5: escolherPagamento(metodo)
UI   --> API : 6: POST /orders/{id}/pay
API  --> PAY : 7: criarCobranca()
PAY  --> GW  : 8: criarCobranca(valor, metodo)
PAY  --> DB  : 9: salvarPagamento(PENDENTE)
GW   --> API : 10: webhook pagamentoConfirmado(txnId)
API  --> PAY : 11: confirmarPagamento(txnId)
PAY  --> DB  : 12: atualizarPedido(PAGO)
PAY  --> Q   : 13: enfileirar(emitir-ingressos)
Q    --> WRK : 14: dispararJob()
WRK  --> TCK : 15: emitirIngressos()
TCK  --> DB  : 16: criarIngressos(qrCodes)
WRK  --> MAIL: 17: enviarEmailIngressos()
MAIL --> BUY : 18: e-mail com QR Code

legend bottom
  Mensagens numeradas indicam a ordem temporal das interações
  entre os objetos colaboradores (notação de comunicação UML).
endlegend

@enduml
